 "amendments": {
  "items": {
   "": {
    "actClause": "AN ACT to amend the highway law, in relation to designating a portion of the\nstate highway system as the \"Trooper James R. Gohery Memorial Bridge\"",
    "basePrintNo": "S6706",
    "basePrintNoStr": "S6706-2023",
    "coSponsors": {
     "items": [],
     "size": 0
    },
    "fullText": "",
    "fullTextFormats": [],
    "fullTextHtml": "",
    "fullTextTemplate": "",
    "lawCode": "Add §344-o, Hway L",
    "lawSection": "Highway Law",
    "memo": " \nBILL NUMBER: S6706REVISED 5/30/23\n\nSPONSOR: RHOADS\n \nTITLE OF BILL:\n\nAn act to amend the highway law, in relation to designating a portion of\nthe state highway system as the \"Trooper James R. Gohery Memorial\nBridge\"\n\n \nPURPOSE OR GENERAL IDEA OF BILL:\n\nDesignates all that portion of the state highway system constituting the\nJerusalem Avenue overpass at the Wantagn State Parkway as the \"Trooper\nJames R. Gohery Memorial Bridge\".\n\n \nSUMMARY OF SPECIFIC PROVISIONS:\n\nSection 1: Amends the highway law by adding a new section 344-p, which\ndesignates all that portion of the state highway system constituting the\nJerusalem Avenue overpass crossing the Wantagh State Parkway in the town\nof Wantagh, county of Nassau, shall be known as the \"Trooper James R.\nGohery Memorial Bridge\".\n\nSection 2: States that the commissioner of transportation shall provide\nfor the installation and maintenance of adequate signing of the state\nhighway systems as designated pursuant to section 1 of this act. The\ndesignation will be for ceremonial purposes only, and the official name\nof the bridge will not be changed as a result of this act.\n\nSection 3: Provides the effective date.\n\n \nJUSTIFICATION:\n\nJames R. Gohery, a proud father and family man, was a State Trooper\nserving at the Bethpage and Wantagh Stations of Troop L who passed away\non December 30th, 1943, while on duty in the village of Freeport. Troop-\ner Gohery was in the process of relaying evidence of a crime to the\nWantagh Station. He is survived by his son James and his descendants. In\n2016, Troop L named their K-9 \"Gohery\" in his honor.\n\nWe cannot forget that our State Troopers serve faithfully in the face of\ngrave danger, with many paying dearly for the safety and comfort we have\ncome to take for granted. This legislation is to pay tribute to Trooper\nGohery's honorable service by memorializing his life and reminding the\npublic of the sacrifices and contributions of our fallen Troopers.\n\n \nPRIOR LEGISLATIVE HISTORY:\n\nS.8927-A of 2021-2022: Passed Senate.\n\n \nFISCAL IMPLICATIONS:\n\nTo be determined.\n\n \nEFFECTIVE DATE:\nThis act shall take effect immediately.\n",
